I’m using the `eng` skill because it owns implementation from already-written tickets. I’ll inspect its exact build and completion behavior, then explain it without changing any files.
## Use `$eng --build`

It treats the written todo tickets as the final implementation specification. It:

- Implements tickets in dependency order.
- Writes and runs unit/integration tests.
- Runs the full test suite, linting, and type checks.
- Automatically launches a separate `$eng --review` agent to review the whole change.
- Resolves serious review findings before continuing.
- Requests approval before committing, including explicit sign-off for database, production configuration, or breaking changes.
- Commits by ticket. In sub-branch mode, it also opens a PR into the feature branch.
- Produces a build summary and hands off to `$pre-merge`.

No files were changed.
